  "semantic_fragments": [
    {
      "fragment_type": "scope_limitation",
      "content": "The Infrared Forehead Thermometer is intended for the intermittent measurement of body temperature from the forehead skin surface on people of all ages. It can be used by consumers in the household environment and by health care providers.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "intended use",
        "forehead thermometer",
        "body temperature",
        "household",
        "health care"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "PT9L",
        "Infrared Forehead Thermometer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "behavioral_spec",
      "content": "The risk management activity including the risk management plan was began at the time the project is approved. The risk management plan has defined the acceptance criteria of risk, and has also arranged the risk management review activity. The risk management group is established to ensure the risk management activity of the current project will be implemented effectively according to the risk management plan. On the development phase and prototype phase of the Infrared Forehead Thermometer, the risk management group reviewed the risk management respectively, and documented the risk management files. The objective of this review is to take a complete evaluation on risk management activity performed on each phase before the product is marketed, to ensure that the risk management plan has been accomplished. And according to evaluating the risk analysis, risk assessment and control, and the acceptance of the residual risk, to ensure that all the risks has been managed and all the residual risk can be accepted.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "risk management plan",
        "risk management activity",
        "risk assessment",
        "residual risk",
        "acceptance criteria"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "PT9L-FXJH01 V1.0",
        "PT9L-FXPJ01 V1.0",
        "PT9L-FXYS01 V1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "constraint_statement",
      "content": "Please find the document Risk Management Plan (PT9L-FXJH01 V1.0) for the risk acceptance criteria.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "risk acceptance criteria",
        "risk management plan"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "PT9L-FXJH01 V1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "behavioral_spec",
      "content": "The risk management group has checked the completion of the Risk Management Plan, and consider that the Risk Management Plan of PT9L has already been accomplished. The residual risk has been reviewed in Verification of risk control measure and Residual Risk Evaluation Report, and the results of the residual risks are accepted.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "risk management plan review",
        "residual risk acceptance",
        "PT9L"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "PT9L-FXJH01 V1.0",
        "PT9L-FXYS01 V1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "behavioral_spec",
      "content": "Please refer to \"Table of getting information of Production and after Production\" from the Risk Management Control Methods (Version: E/0). After the evaluation on the fitness and effectiveness, the risk management Group decided that, the method is appropriate and effective, PT9L can get the information on production and after production with this method, and the Group can perform dynamic risk management when necessary.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "post-production",
        "production information",
        "dynamic risk management",
        "risk management control methods"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "PT9L",
        "Risk Management Control Methods"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "scope_limitation",
      "content": "The Intended use of PT9L is: The Infrared Forehead Thermometer is intended for the intermittent measurement of body temperature from the forehead skin surface on people of all ages. It can be used by consumers in the household environment and by healthcare providers.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "intended use",
        "PT9L",
        "forehead thermometer",
        "body temperature",
        "household",
        "healthcare"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "PT9L"
      ]
    },
    {
      "fragment_type": "design_rationale",
      "content": "Conclusion of Risk Management Review — Overall risk-benefit analysis: From the clinical evaluation report, clinical safety outcomes can prove that the product is safe; clinical performance outcomes can prove that PT9L can achieve its intended use. Users can benefit from proper use, benefits outweigh the overall residual risks, so the overall residual risks are acceptable. Risk Management Group has reviewed the PT9L, and concluded: (1) Risk management plan has been performed properly: The risk management process has been implemented according to the criteria established in the risk management plan standards, the risk team have considered the efficiency and safety of the product, and think that all the identified risks have been controlled as far as possible. (2) Residual risks are acceptable: All single residual risks are in the 'Acceptable' area. And the distribution of all the residual risks less than 1/2 of the overall residual risks are in the higher severity regions or in the higher probability regions. And the clusters of all the residual risks are not borderline. Compared with the intended benefits for PT9L, the benefits outweigh the overall residual risks, so the overall residual risks are also acceptable. (3) The method of getting information of production and after production is proper. In Conclusion, the medical benefits of the intended use outweigh the overall residual risk.",
      "topic_tags": [
        "risk management review",
        "residual risk",
        "risk-benefit analysis",
        "clinical evaluation",
        "acceptable risk",
        "PT9L"
      ],
      "related_subjects": [
        "PT9L",
        "risk management plan",
        "clinical evaluation report"
      ]
    }
  ],
